---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Compare AI Tools & Safe Adoption"
  description="Which AI tool for which office task—Claude, Grok Bot, and ChatGPT compared in plain business English, plus a safe-use checklist."
>
  <section class="hero-bg border-b border-line">
    <div class="container-page py-14">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Tools & adoption</p>
      <h1 class="font-display mt-3 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Which AI tool for which office task?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-ink-muted">
        A practical side-by-side for business owners. Strengths overlap—pick based on the job, your data controls, and what your team will actually use.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-12">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line bg-card shadow-sm">
      <table class="min-w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-paper-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-muted">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">Office task</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-claude">Claude</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-grok">Grok Bot</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-chatgpt">ChatGPT</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-line text-ink-muted">
          <tr>
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Long document / contract review</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — careful reading & risk language</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Useful for summaries & follow-up research</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Solid drafting partner; verify citations</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-paper/40">
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">SOP & policy writing</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — clear structure & tone control</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Good for turning routines into checklists</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — fast structured drafts</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Inbox / calendar triage</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Great for rewriting replies</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — recurring agent-style routines</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Good with custom GPTs / scheduled workflows</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-paper/40">
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Meeting notes → action plans</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Excellent narrative summaries</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Helpful for digests & reminders</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — tables & send-ready emails</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Client proposals</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — polished, careful tone</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Useful for market/competitor add-ons</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — outlines & packaging options</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-paper/40">
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Spreadsheets & formulas</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Good explanations</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Fine for light analysis briefs</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — formula builders & QA checklists</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink">Recurring research digests</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Strong synthesis from long source packs</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4"><strong class="text-ink">Strong fit</strong> — routines + reminders</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-4">Strong drafting of the weekly update</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <a href="/guides/?tool=Claude" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-claude">Claude guides →</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">SOPs, contracts, careful client writing.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/guides/?tool=Grok+Bot" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-grok">Grok Bot guides →</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Inbox triage, calendars, research routines.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/guides/?tool=ChatGPT" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-chatgpt">ChatGPT guides →</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Meetings, proposals, spreadsheet help.</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">More comparisons</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Office tools beyond the chat window</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
        These guides compare products a small office actually buys. Prices and features change, so each one links to the vendor’s current page.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/guides/microsoft-365-copilot-vs-chatgpt-business-vs-claude-team/" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Copilot vs ChatGPT Business vs Claude Team</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Which paid workspace fits a small office that already lives in Microsoft 365, or doesn’t.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/ai-meeting-note-takers-fireflies-otter-teams/" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Fireflies vs Otter vs Teams recap</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Meeting notes from a bot in the call, or from Teams Premium and Copilot.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/zapier-vs-make-office-automation/" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Zapier vs Make</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">How the two automation tools bill, and where an AI step changes the cost.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/secure-ai-office-stack/" class="card hover-card p-5 no-underline">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">A secure AI office stack</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Password manager, business access, admin settings, and data rules that sit under the chat tools.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper-2/50 py-14">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Share with your staff</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">AI Safe-Use Policy Checklist</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
        A concise starter checklist business owners can paste into a handbook or Slack canvas. Customize with your counsel.
      </p>
      <div class="card mt-8 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">1. Prefer business/enterprise plans</strong> for work involving customers, employees, or finances.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">2. Never paste secrets</strong> — passwords, API keys, payroll files, health data, full payment card data, or authentication codes.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">3. Minimize client data</strong> — use initials, sample rows, or redacted excerpts when testing prompts.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">4. Human review before send</strong> — anything client-facing, contractual, or financial gets a named reviewer.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">5. Label AI assistance</strong> when your industry or client agreement expects disclosure.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">6. No autopilot outbound</strong> — do not auto-send email, invoices, or calendar invites without a person clicking send.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">7. Keep a tool allowlist</strong> — Claude, Grok Bot, and ChatGPT (or your approved equivalents) only.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">8. Report incidents quickly</strong> — accidental pastes of sensitive data go to your security/ops owner the same day.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">9. Store finals in company systems</strong> — handbook, Drive, CRM—not only in a chat history.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">10. Retrain quarterly</strong> — refresh examples as products and your policies change.</li>
        </ol>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-primary mt-8"
          data-label="Copy checklist"
          data-copy={`AI Safe-Use Policy Checklist
1. Prefer business/enterprise plans for customer, employee, or financial work.
2. Never paste secrets (passwords, keys, payroll, health data, payment cards, auth codes).
3. Minimize client data; use redactions or sample rows when testing.
4. Human review before anything client-facing, contractual, or financial is sent.
5. Label AI assistance when required by industry or client agreement.
6. No autopilot outbound email, invoices, or invites.
7. Keep an approved-tool allowlist.
8. Report sensitive-data incidents the same day.
9. Store final documents in company systems.
10. Retrain the team quarterly.`}
        >
          Copy checklist
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
